# Coding standards

Follow `CODING_STANDARDS.md` at the repo root before adding or editing code.

- Put tables in `backend/app/models/`, API shapes in `backend/app/schemas/`, and single-value rules in `backend/app/validation/`. Do not mix those jobs in one file.
- One concept per module. A route delegates. A service owns one use case. A model does not import FastAPI.
- Every class and function has a docstring that states the product job and any rule the name hides (tenant ownership, claim exception, nullable column). No comments that restate the next line.
- Enforce uniqueness, ownership, and ranges in the database as well as in Python.
- Do not add a base class, interface, or empty folder until a second caller needs it.
- Never print or commit secrets. `backend/.env` stays untracked.
